## Bottom line

The 3D direction is worthwhile, but the previous draft went too far: it presented conditional estimates as established lemmas. The strongest defensible next paper is a **carefully labeled 3D program/proposition paper**, not yet a theorem claiming a positive continuum mass gap.

The first genuine technical deliverable should be:

$$
\boxed{
\text{Compute the complete finite-block effective action or rigorously bound its full polymer activity norm.}
}
$$

Only after that can $\kappa_0$, $\beta_d$, the KP threshold, and the deficit recursion be stated as proved results.
